      "id": 1,
      "text": "Tecumseh was originally called Frances when it was founded in 1856 by settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://tecumsehne.com/about-tecumseh",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name was changed to Tecumseh after Chief Tecumseh, who was said to have been killed by Johnson during the Battle of the Thames.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tecumseh%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Tecumseh became the county seat of Johnson County in February 1857, when the Nebraska Territorial Legislature designated it.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
